// The **HTML** screen's two panes, and the point of this file is that it is the
// Markdown screen's file with one node name changed.
//
// `text-area` writes `html.source`; `html-view` reads the same property with
// `bind=`. Nothing watches the editor, diffs the text or schedules a re-render:
// the element holding the preview is subscribed to the property, a keystroke
// marks it for rebuild, and the next frame is the parsed page (ADR-0062,
// ADR-0296). A live preview is a binding, whatever the document is written in.
//
// `link=` is the half that has no Markdown equivalent. An anchor in the page
// becomes a `button.link` (ADR-0293) and pressing one calls this valued action
// with the `href` -- so a help pane navigates with no Java between the document
// and the model, and *what* following a link means stays the application's
// (ADR-0298).
//
// `html-view` is also not this application's widget and this document never says
// where it comes from. `goldberry-html` is on the module path, its catalog
// declares the node name, and the inflater finds it through a `uses` -- ADR-0131
// again, for the second widget in the same module.
split-pane id="html-split" position=0.5 first-min=240 second-min=240 {
    column id="html-editor" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "HTML — type here"
        // `fill=#true`, `class="mono"`: the editor half of §4's `text-area`, exactly
        // as the Markdown screen has it. What this is *not* is an HTML editor with
        // tag completion -- that is nobody's plan.
        text-area id="html-source" class="mono" bind="html.source" change="html.set-source" fill=#true
    }
    column id="html-preview" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "Rendered — this side follows"
        // What the last pressed link handed over. A `text` bound to a property the
        // action writes, which is the whole of "the application decides what a link
        // does": the toolkit hands over an href and stops.
        text id="html-followed" class="caption" bind="html.followed"
        scroll {
            html-view id="html-rendered" bind="html.source" link="html.follow" images="app.assets"
        }
    }
}
